#
# Declarative example-conformance fixtures for the inhabitation slice — the
# test-DSL twin of "this counter-example must be rejected with THIS code". The
# gmeow:exampleFile path is SLICE-RELATIVE (resolved against
# slices/core/inhabitation/, not the repo root).
#
# This pins the constant-configuration invariant (INHABITED-COMPETENCY.md CQ2)
# as a TESTED SHACL shape, not an assumption: gmeow:InhabitationConfigurationShape
# constrains gmeow:configurationEmbodiment to sh:maxCount 1, so a configuration
# with two embodiments over one interval MUST be rejected. The
# expectedViolationCode string is the native SHACL finding code
# finding_from_shacl builds as "shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>"
# (crates/validate/src/findings.rs), confirmed by running the harness over the
# counter-example merged with the module + slice shapes.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/inhabitation/tests/> .

# --- Violating: a configuration that changes embodiment without opening a new one.
ex:ecConfigTwoEmbodiments a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/config-two-embodiments.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares one gmeow:InhabitationConfiguration with two gmeow:configurationEmbodiment values over a single interval. gmeow:InhabitationConfigurationShape enforces the constant-configuration invariant via sh:maxCount 1 on gmeow:configurationEmbodiment, so validation MUST emit shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent — a changed embodiment must open a NEW configuration, never a second embodiment on the existing one." .
